comments.body:
@Mulbetty thanks for raising this issue. I think you are right that the assertion introduced by #6979 is problematic. I don't use `mpi` so I have limited experience. But from my brief research, it seems the relevant env vars (e.g., `OMPI_COMM_WORLD_LOCAL_RANK`) ought to be set by `mpirun`. This means these env vars are not required to exist [here](https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/blob/e0a6bb510bf77f5f5b3907da2a76786abe74eef1/deepspeed/launcher/multinode_runner.py#L159) before `mpirun` is invoked.

Commenting out `self._setup_mpi_environment()` as you suggest solves the issue on my side. Perhaps commenting out the assertion is the safer fix here. I will like to get your thoughts. 

@jeffra @sfc-gh-mwyatt any thoughts?
